	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12197"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1" title="View the profile of Kinladar">Kinladar</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Ranger Bait<br />
								Administrator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14456<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12197#msg12197"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12197#msg12197">Re: Stupid People</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #54 on:</b> October 29, 2004, 08:25:39 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I generally vote more conservative, but I feel in this case, Health Care is one of the few things that should NOT be privatized, and should have the strictest oversight to prevent malpractice, penalize doctors who are poor practitioners, and to make sure everyone gets a fair chance at health care.<br /><br />This is one of the few things I think every american has a right to, and with teh current state of the system, only the insurance companies, and trial lawyers are getting any great deal of benefit from our health care system.<br /><br />Right now, the patient comes out on the short end of the stick, unless they have a few million dollars in the bank, and can afford to pay a doctor straight up (IE are not tied to the insurance company telling them what can and can not be done)<br /><br />At the same time, you have some doctors who call for many more tests than are sometimes needed, to pad the bill. <br /><br />America&#039;s Health care system has some really caring people... a doctor I had for about 10 years, retired at 45, due to all the stress of dealing with the Planned Health Care systems, the hospital&#039;s rules, and other issues, trying to care for so many people in our neck of the woods. <br /><br />He was one of the best doctors I have ever seen, and really cared about the patient&#039;s first. My oldest son would have been in alot of trouble if this guy, as a second opinion had not taken to time to listen to us. The first jackoff considered us over-worried first time parents. He totally blew us off.<br /><br />I&#039;m the oldest of four, and helped neighbors watch thier kids when I was growing up, I&#039;ve been around little kids, and knew alot more than most first time parents would. When he blew off my kid&#039;s upchucking everything in his stomach as &quot;wet burps&quot; and sent us home, we just found another doctor. We were at the local medical college the same day, and he was being prepped for surgery the next day, once they got him hydrated.<br /><br />Pyloric Stenosis was the term used, it&#039;s when the valve between the stomach and intestines closes, and won&#039;t open. Common in first born baby boys for some reason, but usually does not manifest till 6-8 weeks of age, our son was 2 weeks old. Youngest case the surgeon (who was a 20 year veteran) had seen.<br /><br />In any event, we were fortunate to find the Doctor when we did, so far everyone else I have taken my family too since is pathetic, and just HMO leaching. We hope to find a real doctor again soon, but the hope gets a little fainter every time we look.<br /><br />Health Care in America needs a major over haul, and the insurance, and doctor&#039;s associations need to be muzzled if it ever happens. It needs to be the patients of the country to help to craft that policy not the people who are the reason it&#039;s so screwed up.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12207"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402" title="View the profile of Callon">Callon</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 381<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Warpig<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12207#msg12207"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12207#msg12207">Re: Stupid People</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #55 on:</b> October 29, 2004, 12:31:26 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Health Care is one of the few things that should NOT be privatized,</div><br />You mean health care insurance, correct?&nbsp; Health care itself is virtually all privatized.&nbsp; I assume you&#039;re not advocating that the health care workers all be employees of the government.&nbsp; <br /><br />Anyway, if the government pays for the bulk of health care expenses, haven&#039;t you effectively turned everything into a cost cutting HMO?&nbsp; You know from experience the problems with much of the HMO care available.&nbsp; It&#039;s hard to get the best care that way.&nbsp; <br /><br />We have a model for socialized medicine on a somewhat smaller scale in Canada (~35 million people).&nbsp; I wonder how well it&#039;s going there, how satisfied people are with it, etc.<br /><br />I&#039;m all for more Americans being insured.&nbsp; What bothers me about Kerry&#039;s plan is he doesn&#039;t seem to have any plan for how to pay for it.&nbsp; He just keeps saying that he&#039;ll repeal the Bush tax cut on people making 200k or more.&nbsp; Well okay, but that would only supply enough revenue to cover about 20% of costs for the health care plan he&#039;s proposed.&nbsp; He&#039;s also claimed he will use that same revenue for other proposed expenses besides the health care initiative.&nbsp; Where&#039;s the money going to come from?&nbsp; Of course Bush spends ridiculous amounts of money too and has driven the deficit to record levels.&nbsp; Kerry claims he will be more fiscally responsible, but the plans he proposes wouldn&#039;t lead to that at all.&nbsp; So both of our real choices for President will drive us far deeper into debt.<br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12208"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1" title="View the profile of Kinladar">Kinladar</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Ranger Bait<br />
								Administrator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14456<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12208#msg12208"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12208#msg12208">Re: Stupid People</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #56 on:</b> October 29, 2004, 01:04:08 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I look at health care as one of those basic needs, that should not be hampered with.<br /><br />Health care used to have several restrictions and regulations that have been taken away over time. Like advertising for Prescription drugs. Ever since that was allowed, the drug companies are spending major dollars on advertising thier produsts, more so than developing them now. <br /><br />Huge cluster fuck of a mess.<br /><br />There needs to be realistic restrictions on trial lawyers, and how much they can profit from representing a person. Too many weak cases thrown at the jury systems anymore. It&#039;s then driving up the insurance costs to even be a doctor. Which then get&#039;s passed along down the line to your employer&#039;s insurance.<br /><br />Now doesn&#039;t that last statement sound like a racket? Insurance companies on both sides of the spectrum soaking up the cash.<br /><br />Sorry, insurance companies are a decent idea, if regulated, but in the recent years with lowered regulations, and total deregulation in some cases, all that has happened, is the Insurance comanies are showing record profits, while employers keep cutting into the Insurance benefits they can provide to thier workers.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12250"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202" title="View the profile of xaanru">xaanru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 74<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								I&#039;m not a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12250#msg12250"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1150.msg12250#msg12250">Re: Stupid People</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #57 on:</b> October 30, 2004, 10:18:43 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> generally vote more conservative, but I feel in this case, Health Care is one of the few things that should NOT be privatized, and should have the strictest oversight to prevent malpractice, penalize doctors who are poor practitioners, and to make sure everyone gets a fair chance at health care.<br /></div><br />Am i to gather this means you are considering Kerry?<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">There needs to be realistic restrictions on trial lawyers, and how much they can profit from representing a person. Too many weak cases thrown at the jury systems anymore. It&#039;s then driving up the insurance costs to even be a doctor. Which then get&#039;s passed along down the line to your employer&#039;s insurance.<br /></div><br />Kerry and Edwards have always opposed tort reform. Two trial lawyers are not going to be the ticket to fix the lawsuit mania problem in this country. In fact, it was an Edwards lawsuit that put 5 of the 6 US manufacturers of flu vaccine out of business. Now where did this vaccine shortage come from?<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
